@page
@model PrivacyModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}
<h1>@ViewData["Title"]</h1>
<br>
<p>Pulse is a student project created for a university course. It is not a real commercial service, and no data entered here is sold, shared, or used for any purpose outside the project. This statement describes how the site would handle your information if it were a live product.</p>
<br>
<h2>Information We Collect</h2>
<p>When you create an account, we collect your name, email address, and a password, which is stored in hashed form and never as plain text. To provide tracking features, we also store the fitness information you choose to enter, such as workouts, exercise duration, distance, sets and reps, body weight, and personal goals. We may also collect basic technical information like your browser type and the pages you visit, to help us keep the site working properly.</p>
<br>
<h2>How We Use Your Information</h2>
<p>We use your information to run your account, display your workout history and progress, calculate statistics and trends, and improve the site's features. We do not use your data for advertising and do not sell it to anyone.</p>
<br>
<h2>Cookies</h2>
<p>Pulse uses essential cookies to keep you signed in and to remember your preferences. We do not use third-party tracking or advertising cookies.</p>
<br>
<h2>Data Sharing</h2>
<p>We do not share your personal information with third parties, except where required by law or where needed to operate the site (for example, a hosting provider that stores our database).</p>
<br>
<h2>Data Security</h2>
<p>We take reasonable steps to protect your information, including password hashing and secure connections (HTTPS). However, no website can guarantee complete security, so please avoid entering sensitive information you would not want stored.</p>
<br>
<h2>Your Choices</h2>
<p>You can view, edit, or delete your workout entries at any time. You can also request that your account and all associated data be permanently deleted by contacting us.</p>
<br>
<h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
<p>Pulse is not intended for children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect information from them.</p>
<br>
<h2>Changes to This Statement</h2>
<p>We may update this statement as the project evolves. Changes will be posted on this page with an updated date.</p>
<br>
<h2>Contact Us</h2>
<p>Questions about this statement can be sent to our professor.</p>